Helios DXVK fork: split immediate-context Map(WRITE_DISCARD) for the UMD's threaded front end

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0017 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

The UMD's threaded front end (guest/windows/docs/d3d11-threaded-frontend.md)
records the immediate context's calls into a ring and replays them on a UMD
worker thread, which is then the only thread that enters this context. A
dynamic buffer's Map(WRITE_DISCARD) must answer the app at once, so it is split
into its two halves:

- HeliosFrontendDiscard (app thread): DiscardSlice from a second local
  allocation cache, m_heliosFrontendCache, created like m_allocationCache for
  immediate contexts. It sets the buffer's current mapped slice, which a later
  Map(WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE) on the app thread returns, and touches no other
  context state. A local cache is single-owner state; the worker keeps
  m_allocationCache.
- HeliosFrontendInvalidate (worker thread, in replay order): the
  EmitCs(invalidateBuffer) and ThrottleDiscard half of MapBuffer.

Nothing changes for callers that do not use the two entry points.

